    <profile name="Black Banner of the Muktarhin" typeId="e3be-1b80-f570-96a1" typeName="Magic Standards" hidden="false" id="7295-e7e3-00a4-41d8">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a34c-cc25-6cb9-95e1">The Black Banner is carried aloft by blind Ibn the beggar boy, who cannot see the peril he is in and so is always in the forefront of battle. When calculating which side wins the combat, all wounds scored by Al Muktar himself count double.


If Al Muktar inflicts two (2) wounds and the remaining Desert Dogs inflict three (3) wounds, their combat score will be seven (7) before adding any additional bonuses as indicated in Rulebook.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Sheikh Shufti" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="2ac0-9c8e-aa69-24b4">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">The Desert Dog&apos;s original leader was Sheikh Shufti, and he fights on as Al Muktar&apos;s right hand man and closest friend. This means the Desert Dogs have two (2) characters who can both issue and accept challenges, and both can lead the unit if required.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Scimitar of Dakisir" typeId="e4d1-790a-ab75-2b57" typeName="Magic Weapons" hidden="false" id="0659-a296-ab33-ef62">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="R" typeId="51c8-c0d6-94db-264c">Combat</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="4f75-25c9-31bd-7074">F+1 (F+2)</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="15e2-fff4-477f-ea26">-1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="57a7-47c0-8d74-d54c"/>
        <characteristic name="Note" typeId="5e5e-34db-1ee0-86">This scimitar is a heirloom of the tribal Sheikhs of the Desert Dogs. It was forged centuries ago in the Kasbah of Dakisir, long ago sacked and ruined by the Undead. The blade is decorated with magical texts inlad in gold.


Thanks to his impressive weapon, Sheikh Ahmed Shufti adds +1 Strength to blows he strikes in a turn he has not been charged and +2 Strength against blows struck in a turn he charges.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Leopoldo di Lucci" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="0155-9b83-8671-8873" page="Regiments of Renown, Warhammer Chronicles 2004, p. 62 (Adapted for Warhammer: The Old World - Tears of Bilbali Edition). By Autrigon Tales.">
